course: dictionary
lesson: 7347
title: Finding meaning from clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «The train leaves from platform 4.» Here a platform is the raised flat place where trains leave from, so people wait there for them.
explain: Read the words around the word. «Every evening an orangutan bends branches into a springy platform and piles leaves on top.» Bends, springy and piles leaves tell you a platform is a flat surface you can build and rest on, a bit like a den made of cushions.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «Power companies build platforms on poles so nests do not touch the wires.» A raised flat surface fits perfectly, so that is the right meaning here.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Platform» means a raised flat area where people or things stand.
fact: At a railway station, the platform is where you wait for and get on trains.
fact: In computers, a platform is a system that programs or games run on; in video games, it can be a ledge you jump between.
fact: On a train platform, you stand behind the yellow safety line.
exercise: «The train leaves from platform 4.» What is a platform here? | A kind of thick shoe | A ticket office window | *A raised flat area where people wait for trains
exercise: «Every evening an orangutan bends branches into a springy platform.» What does platform mean here? | A sunny patch of grass | A deep hole in the ground | *A flat, raised bed built in a tree
exercise: In «power companies build platforms on poles», what tells you a platform is high up? | The word power | *The word poles | The word nests | The word build
test: «Crying on the platform, he wonders about hiding under a seat.» Where is he? | In a shop | Under a bridge | *On a station platform | In a car park
test: Platform shoes have very thick soles. What are platform shoes? | Shoes for swimming | Shoes with no laces | Shoes made of glass | *Shoes with very thick soles
exam: In computers, what does a platform mean? | *A system that programs or games run on | A bird's nest made of twigs | A kind of train ticket | A type of tree
